OpenWings patch 0011: pointer clicks and drag for canvas apps

OpenManus's sandbox browser can click screen coordinates and drag and drop;
canvas based apps (maps, whiteboards, some spreadsheet and design tools)
and drag lists have no element refs to act on.

  * src/browser_identity.py: private_browser accepts the drag action and
    the x, y, to_ref, to_x, to_y arguments (still no raw flags or batches).
  * src/tool_schemas.py: documents them (pixels in the latest screenshot).

wings/browser.py describes whatever is under the pointer the same way it
describes a ref'd element, so the pay/order/send guard applies to pointer
clicks and to both ends of a drag; points inside embedded frames are
refused.

